From: TuxRGB
Subject: [PATCH] RetroidAYN: udev rule printed with backslashes

The Retroid/AYN custom udev rule was escaped twice, so --print-udev-rules
wrote SUBSYSTEM==\"leds\", KERNEL==\"rgb:*\", TAG+=\"uaccess\" with the
backslashes: udev cannot parse that line (and TuxRGB's rule checker,
rightly, refuses the whole file). Escaped once, like the other custom rules.

--- a/Controllers/RetroidAYNController/RetroidAYNControllerDetect_Linux.cpp
+++ b/Controllers/RetroidAYNController/RetroidAYNControllerDetect_Linux.cpp
@@ -134,4 +134,4 @@
 
 REGISTER_DETECTOR("Retroid/AYN RGB", DetectRetroidAYNControllers);
 
-REGISTER_CUSTOM_UDEV_RULE(retroid_ayn_rgb, "Retroid/AYN RGB", "SUBSYSTEM==\\\"leds\\\", KERNEL==\\\"rgb:*\\\", TAG+=\\\"uaccess\\\"");
+REGISTER_CUSTOM_UDEV_RULE(retroid_ayn_rgb, "Retroid/AYN RGB", "SUBSYSTEM==\"leds\", KERNEL==\"rgb:*\", TAG+=\"uaccess\"");
